YNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"9ff3c554a0e2738db8b2302ae971e015d4b4d593d4963c9f12f8e9c2fd455c0b","event_uuid":"e63b6d3b-9848-48e3-af95-d023346124c9","position":{"commit_sha":"8b6d6e8585d6c185637d928817403f48fd0b159d","position":"1794548491214563001-e63b6d3b-9848-48e3-af95-d023346124c9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"3d705fec-b472-45ca-b9ca-e9472648a082","comments":[],"created_at":1794530512856650016,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"57fac59e-88e9-4e11-afee-be5c7ddefd66","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b690-7231-22fe-49e4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py` (antifungal-amenable-mite, Gerrit 3366, merged 73848dd1f40) has 3 defects that affect the numbers it records. All 3 were confirmed against the committed `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json`:\n\n1. **Overlap undercounts pipeline findings.** `_surfaced` reads only `blocking` + `advisory`. The verdict's `advisory` list is already cut at `orchestrator.DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP` (20), and DET advisories count toward that cap; `overflow` is never read. In the recorded run, 3 of 11 rows have exactly 19 non-DET pipeline findings, which is the cap minus the DET advisory. So `pipeline_only` and every overlap total are understated, and each row's count depends on the cap.\n2. **`--resume` mixes stale records.** `main` loads `--out` and `run()` reuses its items by `review_event_uuid` without checking that the saved `corpus_digest`, `corpus` and `match_threshold` match the current run. A changed labels file, `--limit` or threshold silently mixes old per-item records into new results.\n3. **No model or runner is recorded.** `_review_in_fresh_store` drops the verdict that carries `runner`/`model`, so the results cannot say which models produced them. The recorded run used the Anthropic API config while the docs show the Bedrock command, and the file cannot show the difference.\n\n## Plan\n1. **RED first.** In `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py`, add 3 failing tests:\n   - `_surfaced` on a verdict with 1 blocking, 20 `advisory` and 5 `overflow` non-DET findings plus 1 DET advisory returns 26 texts (DET excluded).\n   - `main([... \"--resume\" ...])` against a saved `--out` whose `corpus_digest`, `corpus`, `match_threshold` or `schema_version` differs from the current run returns exit 2, writes a message naming that field to stderr, and reviews no row (the fake runner records no call).\n   - each engine record written by `review_row` carries the verdict's `runner` and `model`; an engine that raised records both as `null`.\n2. **Fix 1.** `_surfaced` reads `blocking` + `advisory` + `overflow`, still skipping `tier == \"DET\"`.\n3. **Fix 2.** A helper `resume_mismatch(saved, current) -> str | None` compares `schema_version`, `corpus`, `corpus_digest` and `match_threshold` and returns the first mismatched field. `main` builds the current header with the existing `_results` field values, and on a mismatch prints `--resume refused: <field> differs (saved=<a>, current=<b>)` to stderr and returns 2 before any review. `schema_version` moves from 1 to 2 because records gain fields, so a v1 file cannot be resumed into a v2 run.\n4. **Fix 3.** `_review_in_fresh_store` copies `runner` and `model` from the final verdict into the engine record (`None` on a raise).\n5. **Docs.** `docs/llm-framework.md` §engine comparison: overlap counts overflow advisories, `--resume` refuses a mismatched header (exit 2), and each record names its runner and model.\n6. **Re-run.** From the change's worktree, with the default Bedrock config: `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison --out src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json` (fresh, no `--resume`), and commit the new results file in the same change. Record the summary on this ticket and, as a dated comment, on epic `pompous-vitriolic-macaw` saying this run supersedes the figures recorded from 73848dd1f40.\n\nNo other behavior change: matching, the threshold, outcome classification, the summary fields and the corpus selection stay as they are. No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Overlap reads `blocking` + `advisory` + `overflow` (non-DET), pinned by a test with more than 20 pipeline advisories.\n- [ ] `--resume` refuses (exit 2, message names the mismatched field) when the saved `schema_version`, `corpus_digest`, `corpus` or `match_threshold` differs, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] Each per-engine record carries the verdict's `runner` and `model`, pinned by a test.\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` describes the overflow counting, the resume refusal and the recorded runner/model.\n- [ ] The committed `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json` has `schema_version` 2, `valid: true`, and every engine record names a runner and model.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The re-run's summary is recorded on this ticket, and a dated comment on `pompous-vitriolic-macaw` says it supersedes the earlier recorded figures.\n  provenance: environment=operator workstation worktree calling Bedrock in account 896586841071 through frontier-bedrock; principal=the operator's frontier AWS identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the comparison measures live model behavior, which no offline fixture reproduces","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py","reason":"overflow, resume check, runner/model"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py","reason":"RED tests for the 3 defects"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"harness behavior"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/engine_comparison_results.json","reason":"re-run with the fixed harness"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"30877e3b-db83-43e9-bc17-ce201651f9ac","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e1f6-d986-5adc-4d0b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Engine comparison undercounts pipeline findings, mixes stale resume records, and records no model","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["11f14638-4d63-41f5-b72d-0e2ea1cb6b98","57fac59e-88e9-4e11-afee-be5c7ddefd66","11673eb6-0013-442b-ace6-170a188a4550","7a3da78a-a3d6-4676-9143-42302bc36856","7a33a990-ac50-4ec5-9043-19fad170c473","30877e3b-db83-43e9-bc17-ce201651f9ac","e63b6d3b-9848-48e3-af95-d023346124c9"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794548491214563002,"uuid":"b6a3cd36-441b-454a-af6d-168ca035d8e5"}